; The CONSUMER shape import mode spells through an ACCUMULATOR: a dependency type in every REPEATED
; position — a list element, a map key and a map value.
;
; `borrow<imported-resource>` is usable only in a NON-REPEATED parameter position: `list<borrow<t>>`
; is legal WIT whose Rust lowering is E0506 (wit-bindgen hoists one handle binding out of the
; lowering loop and reassigns it while a reference is retained), measured unfixed from the pinned
; 0.57.1 through 0.60.0. So each of these parameters is passed as a borrow of a consumer-exported
; accumulator the caller fills one element at a time, and the CBOR seam runs once per element inside
; that filler rather than once per collection at the door.
;
; Compiled, not only read: the shape's whole reason for existing is a macro-expansion failure no WIT
; oracle can see, so this fixture is one of the two consumers the cross-crate `wasm32-wasip2` build
; gate builds.

vault = [
    ; a dependency type as a list element
    items: [* token],
    ; ... as a map key
    keyed: { * token => uint },
    ; ... and as a map value
    valued: { * uint => token },
]
